From 2e8b1cb2b0da45284ea57119600166d807474244 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:57:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(test): give coarse_rims thread_mill the cutting field

PR #1076 added Tool::cutting; the coarse_rims suite reached main in a
separate PR and the merge did not show the compile break. Add
cutting: Vec::new() to the thread_mill Tool literal, as the other Tool
literals got in #1076. No logic change.

Fixes #1349

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/app/tests/coarse_rims.rs | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/crates/app/tests/coarse_rims.rs b/crates/app/tests/coarse_rims.rs
index 7b67d422..ac776df9 100644
--- a/crates/app/tests/coarse_rims.rs
+++ b/crates/app/tests/coarse_rims.rs
@@ -131,6 +131,7 @@ fn thread_mill(diameter: f64) -> Tool {
         holder_len: 35.0,
         material_group: "steel".into(),
         center_cutting: true,
+        cutting: Vec::new(),
         rpm: 6000.0,
         feed: 400.0,
         tool_material: None,
